# Bonny Pall, Clearcutter: "draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand or graveyard" (CR 608.2c). In turn 5
# the trigger draws the Forest and that very card goes onto the battlefield, so the draw came first; Bot2's Plains (binned
# by Entomb in turn 2) is in an opponent's graveyard and can't be chosen. Beau goes 1/1 to 2/2. In turn 7 Bot1 declines:
# the Island drawn stays in hand, Beau stays 2/2. Hand: Dress Down after turn 3; the turn-5 Mountain and the Forest drawn,
# the Forest put 2; the turn-7 Swamp and the Island drawn 4. Then Giant Growth on Beau and Dress Down (CR 613.1f) takes
# Beau's characteristic-defining ability away (CR 604.3): with no other source its power and toughness are 0/0, so 3/3 with
# the Growth; Dress Down's own card puts the hand at 3. Beau is a legendary token and no World (CR 205.4): Bot2's Concordant
# Crossroads, a World enchantment cast in turn 2, stays on the battlefield (CR 704.5k).
# Bonny Pall, Clearcutter {3}{G}{U}{U}: Legendary Creature - Giant Scout 6/5
#   Reach
#   When Bonny Pall enters, create Beau, a legendary blue Ox creature token with "Beau's power and toughness are each
#   equal to the number of lands you control."
#   Whenever you attack, draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand or graveyard onto the battlefield.

